      "text": "# Task 7 controller ruling 24 — reachable knowledge publication prerequisite\n\nRuling: Task7 must resolve the concrete reachable knowledge-publication mutation fence before final acceptance, within its restored generic command; do not merely mark the entire CMS slice code-complete and defer this known dependency. First run focused actual owned-hosted behavior RED against the currenta2 candidate and an inert actual knowledge-handler42501 RED. No helper/body/HTTP amendment until the RED and exact existing modern helper contract are reviewed. Preserve the currenta2 finalDB/Gate2 receipts as historical proven bytes. Minimum intended scope is the existing sorted referenced document-assets published-flag row fence, no new expected-version policy/helper/grant/owner/default or legacy full-file replay; protect existing post→asset lock order, result-not-found priority and transaction audit rollback. A demonstrated HTTP42501 defect gets only the same existing safe403 boundary semantics.\nReason: bounded graph/static trace proves staff/admin POST /api/admin/knowledge→handler/service/repository→generic knowledge_post upsert with isPublished:true, while hosted capture lacks modern private.enforce_published_knowledge_document_assets/helper trigger. Original generic SQL writes is_published and refs with no such row fence. Public reads still filter publishedassetflags and safePDFpaths; no public exposure is demonstrated. The user's binding #130 preservation and R01 compatibility requirements make this a source dependency to fix, rather than a new publication/role policy.\nCost if wrong: an overly broad change could alter error priorities, create asset→post lock-order inversions or falsely claim modern helper absence is safe. Require exact legacy-tail/modern-helper comparison, real valid and invalid referenced-assets behavior and both transaction orders for asset flag changes, missing-target and audit rollback preservation, unchanged modern helper/owner/fullACL/default/native metadata, final frozen compositions/four gates/bindings plus independent review and exact-head5CI. Counts for public146 requirements remain unchanged by this extra fence; production44gaps and all production/release/Task1 boundaries remain unchanged."
