      "evidence": "task-13-brief.md",
      "text": "# Supplemental Task13 — existing document publication guards\n\n## Ruling26 — controlled follow-up, after Tasks8–12\n\nRuling: add a separate source/isolated Task13 before whole-branch review and release packaging to resolve the concrete document inverse-publication prerequisite discovered during Task7. Do not expand the active Task7 implementation or claim its inline knowledge fence repairs later document unpublication. Start with fresh schema-only metadata and actual owned-clone failing behavior for the existing document command/native trigger policy. No new helper/trigger/body/grant changes until the controller has reviewed the actual RED and exact existing modern contracts. Existing-good modern objects get regression verification and must be preserved. Public146 counts are not a complete private/native readiness gate; track supplemental prerequisites explicitly.\n\nReason: actual Task7 v5 hosted capture2026-10-02T02:34:18.064Z has no private.protect_published_document_references helper/trigger, while modern02:34:39.647Z contains the existing postgres-owned SECDEF trigger helper with rawACLnull/default0/search_path empty, bodyMD5e3f2e0627f31f992f350f3b67d71070e/definitionb1b5bdbb2a0156440be3eb784eff93c9. Both schema-only captures prove parity/fullpreservation/normalDROP. Bounded graph/source reads show documentService.unpublishAsset performs reference checks before invoking mutate_document_asset_with_audit, outside its transaction. The historical document command checks annual_reports but the legacy source alone is not proof of the current hosted command's behavior. Task7's asset FOR UPDATE protects its publication transaction, not a later unpublication. This is a named dependency of the user's required #130 preservation and R01 compatibility, not a new policy.\n\nCost if wrong: unnecessary or mismatched native guards could alter valid document publication, block maintenance, introduce lock inversions or widen privileged function access. Require fresh exact actual command/helper/trigger/table/default/native/owner/fullACL/grant-option contracts, meaningful isolated RED before source change, both concurrency orders, valid transitions and audit rollback, final frozen two-profile/gate bindings and independent review. No whole legacy replay, new role/Auth/table/default grants, production DDL/DML, real document publication, paid branch or new release authority. Task1 pending source ACL approval remains separate.\n\n## Requirements (investigation first; minimum repair requires subsequent ruling)\n\n- Work in its own clean isolated branch after accepted Tasks8–12, using their actual final source HEAD/CI gates. Record BASE; index the exact checkout graph. No subagents; no push/merge/provider action.\n- Read current AGENTS/CLAUDE and exact document command/call contracts. Use graph-first discovery; migrations are graph-excluded and may be read directly.\n- Capture schema only, no production rows/actor RPC. Reconstruct fresh guarded zero-data owned clone through the existing harness; Task1 partial SQL excluded. Preserve template/modern fixture, rows/catalog/Auth effective column rights/default ACL/native/ledger and normal DROP. Never change cluster roles or an existing DB/engine.\n- Verify actual mutate_document_asset_with_audit contract rather than assuming its historical body. Review the three existing private/native guards from 20260926150000_guard_published_document_slots.sql and current catalog: enforce_published_site_document_slot_asset, enforce_published_knowledge_document_assets, protect_published_document_references. Verify each actual absence/presence separately; do not infer site-slot absence from the captured inverse-helper absence.\n- Actual RED: an existing published knowledge post/slot referencing a PDF must prevent later unpublication inside the command transaction, with no asset/audit partial commit. Exercise legitimate service/role flow; public reads currently filter published assets, so do not claim observed public exposure. Demonstrate the actual missing guard and any reachable race; existing-good modern behavior is a regression, not a defect.\n- Report RED source/commands/exits/environment/receipt paths and exact modern helper/trigger/function/table/fullACL/default contracts to controller before implementation. No new expected-version, role policy, helper grants or body replacement by analogy. Restoration of a reviewed missing existing policy is the candidate repair, not authorization to replay the whole file or silently normalize existing ACLs.\n- Once ruled: exact bounded forward migration generated by pinned Supabase CLI; fail55000 on unknown metadata before mutation; preserve known modern definitions/native/default/ACL exactly. Test two applies, real behavior, targeted complete-profile negatives after accepted baselines. Include both transaction orders: publication holding asset lock then unpublish waiting and refusal after commit; unpublish first then publication waiting/refusal. Include permitted unpublish after references are unpublished, direct role rejection and audited rollback. No real notification/publication.\n- Bind every new/missing private helper/native trigger as explicit supplemental manifest/runbook/readiness evidence outside the146public target count; leave Task1 five pending public columns and production44 gaps correctly qualified. No overall-ready claim while this supplemental item is open.\n- Focused format first, freeze current executable/runtime inputs, complete own hosted+modern compositions and mandatory typecheck/full tests/lint/build plus applicable DB/RLS tests, retain raw failures and canonical/raw/Git bindings. Archive copied source as *.source with short-path translation; do not cause Bun rediscovery or change runtime receipt paths.\n- Independently review the whole task, then controller prepares a separate DRAFT DO-NOT-MERGE PR with exact-head five individual CI gates. Aggregate CI status is insufficient. Report code-complete/schema-ready-in-isolation/deployed/operationally-enabled separately.\n- In the task's own source/document commit append this controlled supplemental task to the tracked R01 forward plan, without rewriting historical reports; update task tracker/evidence and release manifest/runbook qualifications. Controller may prepare ignored coordination files only.\n\nReport file: same plan-local task-13-report.md. Return only status, commits, one-line actual test summary and concerns.\n"
